9ad","solve/source/generator.py":"14284b3bd817e139cf615486973e192da5ec84a97f50c200832e23cd682551ed","solve/summary.json":"7cb265a4626e1c34022576df381e1d742dccdaf94a9e3e5ff1ee04c78256196b"},"feedback_items":[{"id":"F1","text":"Make small declared schedules self-enumerating in the battery\n\n**Priority: highest shared-tool change.** The ordinary final battery completed every nonsemantic stage but failed semantic gate solely because `LESSON_SCHEDULE_PERIOD=4` had not been explicitly enumerated (`checks/after/checks/b19deac47327_after_battery_summary.json`). A fresh run with `--enumerate-schedule-period --schedule-seed 0` was fully green (`checks/after-enumerated/checks/b19deac47327_after_battery_summary.json`).\n\nFor small declared periods, the battery should automatically enumerate them under strict after/audit policy, or emit the exact `review.py run ... --enumerate-schedule-period` command as a structured next action. This would preserve rigor while avoiding a complete second twelve-stage battery for a known finite schedule receipt."},{"id":"F2","text":"Surface all defect-lint root causes in the compact stage result\n\nThe before battery’s terminal tail emphasized the height-span warning, while the complete log also contained 24 strict public-call findings. The structured battery summary recorded only the stage failure, so the reviewer had to inspect the full log to discover the complete repair scope (`checks/before/checks/b19deac47327_before_defect_lint.log`).\n\nAdd grouped category counts and one minimized witness per category to the battery summary, matching the override checker’s `root_causes` pattern. The terminal tail should print each category once rather than whichever finding happens to be last."},{"id":"F3","text":"Add a reusable parametric-evidence scaffold\n\nThe task-local prototype had to implement recurring plumbing: exact canonical-rule binding, variant Racket generation, protected labeling, independent-mirror checks, public/private episode separation, parameter-rival scoring, canonical replay, and a hash manifest. The result is retained at `repo/generators/b19deac47327/workspace/parametric/prototype.py` with evidence in `checks/parametric/projection-depth-v1/`.\n\nA shared `arcpuzzles parametric-probe` scaffold could accept a canonical rule, a finite parameter table, and an input factory, then produce the same source-bound evidence layout. It should remain authoring-only and never select or approve a variant automatically."}],"packet_id":"ee835cf31b5faa0498e135f699e5f09949b0bd6bf3b943d18a7a0a0152610e41","reviewer_blind_solve":{"attempt_count":1,"attempt_intents":{"solve-blind/attempts/0001/report.json":"solve"},"attempt_reports":["solve-blind/attempts/0001/report.json"],"earlier_rule_exposure":"no","feedback_policy":"visible_only","generator_hash":"a95dfe6dc79eb24c223a6dad735b64117dedae6d0769968e9571bfedbc9a5846","instance_hash":"0c14ccf0e5efae5cfd8e9c1bcf377f8b906442354062e7e492a5fef610cc92cc","reference_consulted_during_solve":false,"solve_kind":"blind_before_repair","source_kind":"reviewer_authored","status":"finished","task_id":"019445e9b5a1"},"reviewer_solve":{"attempt_count":1,"attempt_intents":{"solve/attempts/0001/report.json":"solve"},"attempt_reports":["solve/attempts/0001/report.json"],"earlier_rule_exposure":"yes","feedback_policy":"visible_only","generator_hash":"14284b3bd817e139cf615486973e192da5ec84a97f50c200832e23cd682551ed","instance_hash":"6254956c339a84254c9d3145bcb9628e1a77f2056cb446745b775e2c077310ad","reference_consulted_during_solve":false,"source_kind":"reviewer_authored","status":"finished"},"schema":"arcpuzzles-review-intake-v1","stopping_reason":"Canonical repair, source-bound parametric prototype, required blind and post-repair solves, two adversarial audits, and final verification completed; audit-target defects and prototype approval status are documented without modifying peer sources or Racket authority.","task_id":"b19deac47327","training_admitted":false,"verification_command